{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_011CfcuzKh3NUhZkemb1MGrh","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"VERDICT: LGTM\n\nThe change is coherently placed and idiomatic for this class:\n\n- **Right unit.** `OwnerTelephone` already owns \"normalize to E.164 and return null if the result isn't valid E.164.\" The national-length-per-country rule is another facet of that same validity judgment, so extending this class (rather than introducing a separate validator) is the natural home. The new rule layers on top of the existing `E164.matches()` check rather than tangling with it.\n\n- **No catch-all growth.** The new logic is factored into a focused private helper `hasValidNationalLength(...)` with its own Javadoc, keeping `normalize(...)` readable (fail-fast on the general rule, then delegate). The method does one thing.\n\n- **Data vs. logic separation is clean.** Per-country lengths live in the `NATIONAL_LENGTHS` table, so adding a country is a one-line data edit, not a code change. The static initializer block is the conventional way to build an unmodifiable-intent constant map here.\n\n- **The `LinkedHashMap` choice is documented with its reason** (prefix-ordering so a longer code wins over a shorter prefix), which is exactly the kind of non-obvious intent a maintainer would want recorded.\n\n- **Javadoc kept in sync.** The class-level doc was updated to describe the new rule and the \"unrecognized code passes on the general rule alone\" behavior, matching the implementation — no stale contract left behind.\n\nNothing is duplicated, and a maintainer of this codebase would find the shape natural."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":9920,"cache_read_input_tokens":11894,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":9920},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_